-          <details class="about-section" open>
-            <summary>About</summary>
-            <h1>Free Online Pool, Snooker &amp; Billiards Game</h1>
-            <p>
-              Play free online pool, snooker and carom billiards with
-              <a
-                href="https://github.com/tailuge/billiards"
-                target="_blank"
-                rel="noopener"
-                >Tailuge Billiards</a
-              >, an open-source 3D cue sports simulator. Play 8-ball, 9-ball,
-              snooker and three-cushion billiards directly in your browser on
-              desktop or mobile. No download, installation or account required.
-              Practise shots, challenge other players or explore realistic ball
-              motion, spin and cushion rebounds.
-            </p>
-            <p>
-              The game uses a physics engine based on published research into
-              billiard-ball motion, collisions and cushion impacts. Adjust your
-              aim, spin and shot power, experiment with different positions, and
-              study how the cue ball moves around the table.
-            </p>
-
-            <h2>Pool, Snooker and Carom Games</h2>
-            <ul>
-              <li>
-                <a href="eightball">8-ball pool</a>. Play the classic
-                solids-and-stripes pool game with realistic ball physics and a
-                high-resolution rendering mode.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="nineball">9-ball pool</a>. Play the fast-paced rotation
-                game, practise custom table layouts, and share replay links to
-                review interesting shots.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="snooker">Snooker</a>. Play snooker on a full-size
-                12-foot table with 15 reds, or practise on a smaller 6-foot
-                table. Practise potting, cue-ball positioning and
-                break-building.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="threecushion">Three-cushion billiards</a>. Play
-                3-cushion carom, where the cue ball must contact both object
-                balls, reaching at least three cushions before contacting the
-                second object ball. Explore spin, rebound angles and cue-ball
-                paths with a physics model developed for realistic cushion
-                behaviour.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="?ruletype=sagu">Sagu (Korean four-ball)</a>. Play the
-                Korean four-ball carom game on a standard or smaller 5-foot
-                table.
-              </li>
-            </ul>
-            <p>
-              Two practice bots, ClawBreak and TheFarJaw, play when nobody else
-              is around; the
-              <a href="speedrun/">speedrun challenge</a> races you against the
-              clock, and the <a href="reveal/">reveal game</a> uncovers pictures
-              with straight-pool potting.
-            </p>
-
-            <h2>Realistic billiards physics</h2>
-            <p>
-              This online billiards simulator models how balls roll, collide,
-              spin and rebound from the cushions. Its physics follow published
-              research on ball motion and cushion impacts. Explore ball-to-ball
-              collisions, throw, spin and cushion rebounds, and see how these
-              effects change the path of a shot. Ball motion follows
-              <a
-                href="https://billiards.colostate.edu/physics_articles/Han_paper.pdf"
-                target="_blank"
-                rel="noopener"
-                >Han (2005)</a
-              >
-              with corrections noted by
-              <a
-                href="https://ekiefl.github.io/2020/04/24/pooltool-theory/#3-han-2005"
-                target="_blank"
-                rel="noopener"
-                >Kiefl</a
-              >; ball-to-ball collisions follow
-              <a
-                href="https://billiards.colostate.edu/technical_proofs/new/TP_A-14.pdf"
-                target="_blank"
-                rel="noopener"
-                >Alciatore</a
-              >, including the throw effect; and cushion impacts use
-              <a
-                href="https://billiards.colostate.edu/physics_articles/Mathavan_IMechE_2010.pdf"
-                target="_blank"
-                rel="noopener"
-                >Mathavan (2010)</a
-              >, with Stronge's compliant-cushion model available as an
-              alternative. Spin, throw and cushion rebound can all be inspected
-              and re-tuned on the
-              <a href="diagrams/three">three-cushion physics page</a>.
-            </p>
-
-            <h2>Pool, Snooker and Billiards Practice</h2>
-            <ul>
-              <li>
-                <a href="practice">Billiards practice table</a>. Set up custom
-                shots and ball positions, then repeat them to practise aim, spin
-                and cue-ball control without an opponent or a time limit.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="exam/">Billiards skill tests</a>. Work through a graded
-                series of shots and receive an assessment level, completion
-                status and score.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="exam/snooker">Snooker practice and assessment</a>. Work
-                through a graded course of snooker shots, from basic pots to
-                difficult positions.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="exam/threecushion"
-                  >Three-cushion practice and assessment</a
-                >. Practise carom shots across a graded series, from basic
-                positions to advanced cushion routes.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="fit/research">Shot sensitivity analysis</a>. See how
-                aim, spin, power and elevation change the result.
-              </li>
-              <li>
-                <a href="diagrams/diamond">The diamond system</a> for
-                three-cushion cue-ball paths.
-              </li>
-            </ul>
-
-            <h2>Online Multiplayer Pool and Billiards</h2>
-            <p>
-              Play online billiards against other players. The
-              <a href="lobby">multiplayer lobby</a> shows who is online and lets
-              you challenge available opponents. Use
-              <a href="2tab">two-tab mode</a> to play across two windows on one
-              device, or join <a href="arena">scheduled arenas</a> for timed
-              tournaments. High breaks appear on the
-              <a
-                href="https://scoreboard-tailuge.vercel.app/leaderboard"
-                target="_blank"
-                rel="noopener"
-                >leaderboard</a
-              >
-              and rated games contribute to your
-              <a
-                href="https://scoreboard-tailuge.vercel.app/elo"
-                target="_blank"
-                rel="noopener"
-                >Glicko-2 rating</a
-              >.
-            </p>
-
-            <h2>Guides and Billiards Research</h2>
-            <ul>
-              <li>
-                <a href="blog1">Why most pool games feel wrong</a>: what makes a
